WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.660
SPEAKER Hello.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.410
Today we're excited to announce
the beta of Security Health

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.680
Analytics, a security product
that integrates into Cloud

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.840
Security Command Center.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:13.260
Security Health Analytics helps
you identify misconfiguration

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.290
and compliance violations in
your Google Cloud Platform

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:19.050
resources and take action.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:22.600
Security Command Center now
has a new Vulnerabilities tab.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.310
When you click the
Vulnerabilities tab,

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.890
you will be taken
to a dashboard that

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.590
summarizes vulnerability
findings identified

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.960
by Security Health Analytics.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.510
If you haven't yet enabled
Security Health Analytics,

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.350
the first time you
land on this page,

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.620
you will be presented
with a message indicating

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.260
that you need to enable Security
Health Analytics in order

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.150
to see vulnerabilities.

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.550
You can click Manage
Security Sources,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.950
which links to the
Security Sources Management

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:51.690
page, where you can enable
Security Health Analytics.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.700
After you enable Security
Health Analytics,

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.860
a preliminary scan
is kicked off.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.490
Within a few minutes,
findings, our word for results,

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.410
will begin to be
published and available

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:04.410
in the Vulnerabilities
dashboard.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.050
At this point, you can visit
the Vulnerabilities tab again,

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.650
and you will be presented
with the misconfigurations

00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.730
that Security Health
Analytics has detected.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.720
Misconfigurations are presented
as a table of recommendations.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:19.710
These recommendations are
sorted by their severity.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.450
Each recommendation
is associated

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.490
with an individual finding type.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:26.520
For example, the firewall
rules recommendation

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:29.670
is associated with the
open firewall finding type.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:31.530
The Active column
shows the number

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:33.660
of currently active findings.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.790
The Status column shows
the current status

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.380
of the detector that
produced the finding.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.500
If you mouse over
the Status icon,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.590
a hint is displayed that
indicates when the scan last

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.030
finished running.

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:46.770
The Benchmark column
currently shows

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.800
which CIS benchmark each
recommendation is associated

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:50.380
with.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:54.900
For example, open RDP port
is associated with CIS GCP

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.170
foundation benchmark 3.7.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.810
Sometimes you'll have a lot
of projects, many of which

00:02:00.810 --> 00:02:02.010
are test projects.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:04.590
It is important to be able
to show active findings

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.690
over a subset of projects.

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.780
For these use cases, the
Vulnerabilities dashboard

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.700
has a projects filter.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:14.070
You can click on the Plus
button to add a project

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.800
to the projects filter.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.750
Let's select API Test.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.810
You can add more than one
project to the project's filter

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.440
and see all of the active
findings in either project.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.590
Here we can see
96 active findings

00:02:28.590 --> 00:02:32.190
for open firewall across
the project's API test

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.950
and buckets without
object versioning.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:37.380
You can click on Open
Firewall, and you'll

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.260
be taken to the Findings
tab, with the correct filters

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.290
applied so that you can see
the individual open firewall

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:46.840
findings for just the
projects selected.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.630
If you click on one
of the findings,

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:50.640
you will be presented
with a Finding Detail

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.790
page that provides an overview
of the problem, as well

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:56.430
as a step-by-step
remediation guide.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.360
From here you can click directly
on the firewall rule, which

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.820
opens the page in another tab.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.640
This allows you to go
back to the previous tab

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.100
to see the remaining
instructions.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.290
Start using Security
Command Center today

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:11.910
and enable Security
Health Analytics

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.680
to help prevent
misconfigurations

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.500
and compliance violations
in your GCP projects.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.050
Thanks.

